    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0782" n="686" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg686"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins Papers</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President’s Special Assistant</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Hopkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President
                    </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d358-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yalta</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-02-06">February 6, 1945.</date>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>
                </p>
                <p>Why not let this wind up today when Stalin
                    is thru—and say we will talk it over again tomorrow. It is 7.15</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d358-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d358-f1-content">
                <p>This note is undated, but the content indicates that it was passed to the
                    President during Stalin’s extended
                    statement on the Polish question during the Third Plenary Meeting on February 6,
                    1945. See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg670">p.
                    670</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
